# operator_orderby.skill — CDLC Context Package
# KQLBridge v0.1 | Generate → Test → Distribute → Observe
# ============================================================

## What order by / sort by does in KQL
Sorts the result set. `sort by` is an alias for `order by`.
Default direction when omitted: asc (Spark SQL default).

## Translation table
| KQL                                 | Spark SQL                             |
|-------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| T | order by ts desc                | SELECT * FROM T ORDER BY ts DESC      |
| T | order by ts asc                 | SELECT * FROM T ORDER BY ts ASC       |
| T | sort by name                    | SELECT * FROM T ORDER BY name ASC     |
| T | order by a desc, b asc          | SELECT * FROM T ORDER BY a DESC, b ASC|

## Full examples
```kql
SecurityEvent | order by TimeGenerated desc | take 100
```
```sql
SELECT *
FROM SecurityEvent
ORDER BY TimeGenerated DESC
LIMIT 100
```

## Edge cases
- Direction keyword absent → defaults to ASC
- `sort by` keyword accepted (grammar alias)
- Numeric column expression: `order by count desc` after summarize works correctly

## Known limits
- `nulls first` / `nulls last` modifiers → not supported in v0.1
- `top N by col desc` shorthand → not in v0.1 grammar; use `order by + take`

## Routing rules
- order_op / sort_op → SUPPORTED → SparkSQLGenerator._order()
- ORDER_DIR named terminal → preserved in parse tree as Token
